#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:82
msgid "Create / update the application's Activity that will be hosting the Godot Engine instance. For the sample app, this is `MainActivity <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/blob/master/apps/gltf_viewer/src/main/java/fhuyakou/godot/app/android/gltfviewer/MainActivity.kt>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:84
msgid "The host Activity should implement the `GodotHost interface <https://javadoc.io/doc/org.godotengine/godot/latest/org/godotengine/godot/GodotHost.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:85
msgid "The sample app uses `Fragments <https://developer.android.com/guide/fragments>`_ to organize its UI, so it leverages `GodotFragment <https://javadoc.io/doc/org.godotengine/godot/latest/org/godotengine/godot/GodotFragment.html>`_, a fragment component provided by the Godot Android library, to automatically host and manage the Godot Engine instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:110
msgid "The Godot Android library provides `GodotActivity <https://javadoc.io/doc/org.godotengine/godot/latest/org/godotengine/godot/GodotActivity.html>`_, an abstract Activity component that can be extended to automatically host and manage the Godot Engine instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:112
msgid "And the embedded Godot project provides `GodotApp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/android/java/app/dataLib/src/main/java/com/godot/game/GodotApp.java>`_, an implementation of ``GodotActivity`` that can be used as a ready standalone Activity to launch and manage the embedded Godot project in its own separate Activity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:116
msgid "Alternatively, applications can directly create a `Godot <https://javadoc.io/doc/org.godotengine/godot/latest/org/godotengine/godot/Godot.html>`_ instance, host, and manage it themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:118
msgid "Using `GodotHost#getHostPlugins(...) <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/blob/master/apps/gltf_viewer/src/main/java/fhuyakou/godot/app/android/gltfviewer/MainActivity.kt#L55>`_, the sample app creates a `runtime GodotPlugin instance <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/blob/master/apps/gltf_viewer/src/main/java/fhuyakou/godot/app/android/gltfviewer/AppPlugin.kt>`_ that's used to send :ref:`signals <doc_signals>` to the embedded Godot project scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:120
msgid "The runtime ``GodotPlugin`` can also be used by the embedded Godot project scripts to access methods from the host Android project. For more information, see :ref:`Godot Android plugins <doc_android_plugin>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/embedding_in_android_projects.rst:122
